(1,1,1,'Oral Communication in Context: Which statement best describes the main topic of this subject?','It focuses on applying and understanding key concepts.','It focuses only on memorization.','It has no practical application.','It is unrelated to the subject.','A'),
(2,1,2,'Oral Communication in Context: Which study practice is most appropriate for this subject?','Review concepts and apply them to examples.','Skip all exercises.','Memorize without understanding.','Avoid reviewing mistakes.','A'),
(3,1,3,'Oral Communication in Context: What is generally the best way to evaluate an answer or solution?','Check it against the concept, process, and available evidence.','Assume the first answer is correct.','Ignore the question requirements.','Choose randomly.','A'),
(4,1,4,'Oral Communication in Context: When solving a subject-related problem, what should a student do first?','Identify what is being asked and the relevant information.','Submit immediately.','Ignore the given information.','Guess without reading.','A'),
(5,1,5,'Oral Communication in Context: Which behavior supports effective learning?','Participating, practicing, and reviewing feedback.','Avoiding practice.','Ignoring feedback.','Relying only on guesses.','A'),
